  "title": "Erdős Problem #805",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For which functions $g(n)$ with $n>g(n)\\geq (\\log n)^2$ is there a graph on $n$ vertices in which every induced subgraph on $g(n)$ vertices contains a clique of size $\\geq \\log n$ and an independent set of size $\\geq \\log n$?\nIn particular, is there such a graph for $g(n)=(\\log n)^3$?",
